- rulings.md: K108(5) filings R9 claim deadlines use holiday calendar (N72); K611 confirmed defects (deadlineRecheck uncalled; no holidays) -> T18; K613; K719 scheduler deadline-recheck built; K841; K921; K925 employer paid holidays read as closure days; HVA left undetermined; K934; K936(3) holidays keyed by year only ignoring offices -> fixed; **K941: City 09-09/11-11 left out => counted as business days "(it errs early, the safe side for a group's deadline)"** — but for a COUNTERPARTY deadline erring early accuses the body prematurely => need direction-aware conservatism; K1000; K1051 volatility.
## Step 7: web research (searches run, findings with URLs)
- CPRA computation: CCP §12 "excluding the first day and including the last, unless the last day is a holiday" -> next business day; FAC: 10 days begin day after receipt; calendar days. https://firstamendmentcoalition.org/2009/06/when-does-the-10-days-count-start-with-a-cpra-request ; https://firstamendmentcoalition.org/2015/09/aa-cpra-ten-day-deadline-for-request-responses-is-that-business-days-or-calendar-days (404 on fetch; search snippet) ; city practice e.g. https://www.losaltosca.gov/169/California-Public-Records-Act . => Mar 19 + 10 = Sun Mar 29 -> Mon Mar 30 matches RM. Built computeDeadline would answer Mar 29 (no roll-forward) => would accuse city a day early.
- FRCP 6(a): exclude trigger day, count all days, last day weekend/holiday -> next day; hours periods; clerk's office inaccessible extends. https://www.courtrules.net/federal/civil-procedure/rule-6 => rule families: roll-forward, hours, inaccessibility.
- FOIA 20 working days excl Sat/Sun/federal holidays; unusual circumstances +10 working days by written notice with date certain; tolling once for info from requester. https://foia.blogs.archives.gov/2011/09/29/twenty-days-or-not ; https://www.law.cornell.edu/cfr/text/5/10000.8 => tolling needed.
- Brown Act: regular meeting agenda 72 h before (Gov Code 54954.2), special 24 h (54956). leginfo AB 2257. https://www.leginfo.ca.gov/pub/15-16/bill/asm/ab_2251-2300/ab_2257_bill_20160411_amended_asm_v98.htm ; Oakland Sunshine Ordinance: regular 72 h (OMC 2.20.080), special 48 h "not counting weekends or holidays" (OMC 2.20.070) https://www.oaklandca.gov/Government/Boards-Commissions/Public-Ethics-Commission/Open-Government/Open-Meetings => notice rules count BACKWARD from an event, in HOURS, with business exclusions; local rule stricter than state.
- Government Claims Act Gov Code 911.2: 6 months after accrual (injury), 1 year other; condition precedent to suit. https://california.public.law/codes/ca_gov't_code_section_911.2 => claim windows start at accrual (act/known).
- RFC 5545 RRULE: FREQ=MONTHLY;BYDAY=2TU; BYSETPOS; https://www.icalendar.org/iCalendar-RFC-5545/3-3-10-recurrence-rule.html
- EDTF / ISO 8601-2:2019: uncertainty, approximation, unspecified digits, intervals, levels 0-2. https://www.loc.gov/standards/datetime/
- OCD Event: start_time tz-qualified, timezone, end_time, all_day, status {cancelled, tentative, confirmed, passed}, agenda, media, documents, participants. https://open-civic-data.readthedocs.io/en/latest/data/event.html
- Legistar Web API GET v1/{Client}/Events https://webapi.legistar.com/Help (public data API; Oakland uses Legistar per corpus).
- Akoma Ntoso lifecycle eventRef (generation, amendment, repeal) + timeInterval start/end refer to events; temporalGroup. https://docs.oasis-open.org/legaldocml/akn-core/v1.0/os/part2-specs/os-part2-specs_xsd_Element_timeInterval.html
- SQL:2011 / bitemporal: valid time vs transaction time; AS OF SYSTEM TIME. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SQL:2011 ; https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transaction_time
- OCDS Period {startDate, endDate, maxExtentDate, durationInDays}. https://standard.open-contracting.org (via prozorro docs https://prozorro-api-docs.readthedocs.io/en/latest/standard/util.html)
- Fiscal years: 46 states July 1; NY Apr 1, TX Sep 1, AL & MI Oct 1; federal Oct 1; CA cities choose (5 use federal FY). https://legalclarity.org/how-state-fiscal-years-work-dates-and-budget-cycles/ ; https://www.leginfo.ca.gov/pub/09-10/bill/asm/ab_2651-2700/ab_2663_cfa_20100817_161925_sen_floor.html
- Temporal taggers: HeidelTime normalization ~77.6 F1 TempEval-3; SUTime 70.3% value accuracy. https://aclweb.org/aclwiki/Temporal_Information_Extraction_(State_of_the_art) => machine date extraction must be a graded proposal, never fact.
- Everlaw Storybuilder fact timelines each fact backed by evidence. https://support.everlaw.com/hc/en-us/articles/42469701435803
- MuckRock tracks requests past due. https://www.muckrock.com/about/how-we-work/
- Auditor follow-up: Seattle tracks 928 recs since 2007; San Diego semiannual with target implementation dates. https://seattle.gov/cityauditor/recommendations ; https://www.sandiego.gov/sites/default/files/recommendation_follow_up_report_ending_june_30_2023.pdf
- Consent decree monitoring: Chicago missed 37 of 50 deadlines (monitor report). https://news.wttw.com/2019/11/15/federal-monitor-cpd-lagging-behind-consent-decree-compliance ; Seattle consent decree timeline https://www1.seattle.gov/police/consent_decree_timeline
- Holiday libraries: date-holidays npm (rules for 199 countries, substitute days, TZ) https://unpkg.com/date-holidays@3.33.0/README.md ; OpenHolidays API https://public-api.org/api/1463/openholidays-api => usable as RESEARCH aids only (doctrine: holiday list belongs to its publisher; secondary not a source).
- Runtime: DO single alarm per object, at-least-once, retries exp backoff 6x https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/api/alarms/ ; Workers Paid CPU 30 s default / 5 min max, 128 MB, alarms 15 min wall https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits/ ; Temporal in Chrome 144 / V8 (Node 26 enabled, V8 14.6) https://www.infoq.com/news/2026/02/chrome-temporal-date-api ; https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v26.0.0 ; Workers changelog V8 14.6-14.8 https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/changelog/ (no explicit Temporal flag found => measure).
- tzdata 3 releases in 2026 (a,b,c) incl BC, Alberta permanent time https://www.iana.org/time-zones/releases => zone rules change; runtime ICU must be current; record tz version.
